        "original_id": "334339b8-a14c-5704-8c6c-40ce5876679d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gatwick Airport, Heathrow Airport, Coldwaltham, Amberley Wild Brooks, Central London, Crawley, Amberley, Greatham Bridge\n- Products/Systems: IATA codes, ICAO codes, Wey South Path\n\nFacts:\n- Gatwick Airport, also known as London Gatwick, has IATA code LGW and ICAO code EGKK.\n- Gatwick Airport is a major international airport in south-east England, 29.5 miles south of Central London and 2.7 nautical miles north of Crawley.\n- Gatwick Airport is the second-busiest airport in the United Kingdom by total passenger traffic, after London Heathrow.\n- Heathrow Airport, also known as London Heathrow, has IATA code LHR and ICAO code EGLL.\n- Heathrow Airport is a major international airport in London, United Kingdom.\n- Coldwaltham is around a 30-minute drive from Gatwick Airport.\n- A path that forms part of the Wey South Path leads through Amberley Wild Brooks from Amberley to Greatham Bridge near Coldwaltham.",
